  enabled: boolean;
  /** Which upstream configuration is in force. `active`: an address for the configured upstream has been checked and approved, and requests are sent through it — this reports the configuration, NOT that the upstream is reachable, so a permitted address with nothing listening on it stays `active` while requests fail. `unavailable`: an upstream has no approved address (refused, not resolvable, the configured text does not parse, or the persisted setting could not be read), so proxied requests are answered `502 configured upstream proxy is unavailable` and are never sent directly instead; the retry continues in the background. `direct`: no upstream is configured and requests are sent directly. */
